binCV -- E-8 / X-14: horizontal decimation by two
three routes to the same destination; 4 inputs, 9 interleaved batches, 40 ms budget
aux B is the mask table plus the scratch row -- built ONCE per width, which is
the most favourable accounting variant C can have

=== 640x480 -> 320x240 ===
  all three variants match the per-pixel reference and each other
  working set of one call: 28800 B read + written at uint32_t, 28800 B at uint64_t

  variant                  ns/dst-pixel min/med/max    spread     aux B       GB/s
  gather uint32_t         4.0181/ 4.0188/ 4.0232      0.1%         0       0.09
  unshuffle uint32_t      0.2750/ 0.2750/ 0.2755      0.2%         0       1.36
  frame-masked uint32_t   3.0773/ 3.0938/ 3.1088      1.0%      1408       0.12
  gather uint64_t         4.8785/ 4.8823/ 4.8856      0.1%         0       0.08
  unshuffle uint64_t      0.1847/ 0.1847/ 0.1850      0.2%         0       2.03
  frame-masked uint64_t   1.5415/ 1.5416/ 1.5434      0.1%      1408       0.24

  variant                    x slower   vs fastest
  gather uint32_t              21.76x             
  unshuffle uint32_t            1.49x             
  frame-masked uint32_t        16.75x             
  gather uint64_t              26.43x             
  unshuffle uint64_t            1.00x   <- fastest
  frame-masked uint64_t         8.35x             

